---
import "../styles/global.css";
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en" data-theme="dark">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />
    
    <!-- SEO Meta Tags -->
    <title>FAQ — AttendEase Attendance Tracker</title>
    <meta name="description" content="Frequently asked questions about AttendEase free attendance tracker. Learn how to use the bunk calculator, mark attendance, and more." />
    <meta name="keywords" content="FAQ, help center, attendance tracker questions, how to use, troubleshooting" />
    <meta name="robots" content="index, follow" />
    
    <!-- Open Graph -->
    <meta property="og:type" content="website" />
    <meta property="og:title" content="FAQ — AttendEase" />
    <meta property="og:description" content="Get answers to common questions about AttendEase attendance tracker." />
    
    <!-- Canonical -->
    <link rel="canonical" href="https://atteendease.com/faq" />
    
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin />
    <link
      href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Inter:wght@300;400;500;600;700&family=JetBrains+Mono:wght@400;500&display=swap"
      rel="stylesheet"
    />
  </head>
  <body class="min-h-screen bg-bg-primary text-text-primary font-sans">
    <!-- Navigation -->
    <nav class="fixed top-0 left-0 right-0 z-50 bg-bg-secondary/80 backdrop-blur-xl border-b border-border">
      <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 h-16 flex items-center justify-between">
        <a href="/" class="flex items-center gap-2">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-md bg-accent flex items-center justify-center">
            <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-white" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
              <path d="M9 11l3 3 8-8"></path>
              <path d="M21 12v7a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V5a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h11"></path>
            </svg>
          </div>
          <span class="text-lg font-semibold tracking-tight">AttendEase</span>
        </a>
        <div class="flex items-center gap-4">
          <a href="/about" class="text-sm text-text-secondary hover:text-text-primary transition-colors">About</a>
          <a href="/contact" class="text-sm text-text-secondary hover:text-text-primary transition-colors">Contact</a>
          <a href="/privacy" class="text-sm text-text-secondary hover:text-text-primary transition-colors">Privacy</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </nav>

    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 py-24">
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-bold mb-4">Frequently Asked Questions</h1>
      <p class="text-lg text-text-secondary mb-12">Common questions about AttendEase attendance tracker</p>
      
      <div class="space-y-4">
        <div class="card p-6">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-3">How do I set up AttendEase?</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-text-secondary">First, click "Get Started" on the homepage. You'll be guided through a simple setup process where you can add your courses, set up your weekly timetable, and configure attendance targets. The entire process takes less than 5 minutes.</p>
        </div>
        
        <div class="card p-6">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-3">Is my data private?</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-text-secondary">Yes! All your attendance data is stored locally in your browser's localStorage. We don't collect, store, or transmit any of your data to external servers. Your attendance records are completely private and accessible only to you.</p>
        </div>
        
        <div class="card p-6">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-3">How does the bunk calculator work?</h3>
          <p class="text-text-secondary">The bunk calculator analyzes your current attendance across all courses and calculates how many classes you can safely skip while maintaining your target attendance percentage. It also provides what-if scenarios to help you plan ahead.</p>
        </div>
        
        <div class="card p-6">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-3">Can I add extra classes?</h3>
          <p class="text-text-secondary">Yes! You can add extra classes for any date using the "Add Extra Class" button in the Mark Attendance page. This is perfect for makeup classes, lab sessions, or other ad-hoc classes not in your regular timetable.</p>
        </div>
        
        <div class="card p-6">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-3">Can I edit past attendance?</h3>
          <p class="text-text-secondary">Yes, you can navigate to any past date using the date picker or navigation buttons and change the attendance status. The update will be saved immediately to your local storage.</p>
        </div>
        
        <div class="card p-6">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-3">What if I clear my browser data?</h3>
          <p class="text-text-secondary">Clearing browser data (cache, cookies, localStorage) will delete all your attendance records. We recommend using the "Export Data" feature in Analytics to backup your data before clearing browser storage.</p>
        </div>
        
        <div class="card p-6">
          <h3 class="text-semibold mb-3">Does AttendEase work offline?</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-text-secondary">Yes! Since all data is stored locally in your browser, AttendEase works perfectly offline. You can mark attendance and access all features without an internet connection.</p>
        </div>
        
        <div class="card p-6">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-3">Is AttendEase really free?</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-text-secondary">Yes, AttendEase is completely free with no subscriptions, premium features, or hidden costs. All features are available to everyone at no charge.</p>
        </div>
        
        <div class="card p-6">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-3">Can I use AttendEase on mobile?</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-text-secondary">Yes! AttendEase is fully responsive and works perfectly on mobile devices. The interface is optimized for touch interactions and provides the same experience as on desktop.</p>
        </div>
        
        <div class="card p-6">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-3">How do I export my data?</h3>
          <p class="text-text-secondary">Go to the Analytics page and click "Export Data" in the Data Management section. This will download a JSON file with all your attendance records that you can keep as a backup.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Footer -->
    <footer class="py-8 px-4 sm:px-6 border-t border-border">
      <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-center justify-between gap-4">
        <a href="/" class="flex items-center gap-2">
          <div class="w-6 h-6 rounded-md bg-accent flex items-center justify-center">
            <svg class="w-4 h-4 text-white" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
              <path d="M9 11l3 3 8-8"></path>
              <path d="M21 12v7a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V5a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h11"></path>
            </svg>
          </div>
          <span class="text-sm font-medium">AttendEase</span>
        </a>
        <p class="text-xs text-text-muted">© 2026 AttendEase. Free attendance tracker for students.</p>
      </div>
    </footer>

    <style>
      body {
        font-family: 'Inter', system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif;
      }
    </style>
  </body>
</html>
